      "writtenOn": "2024-08-29T16:52:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What I imagine is, *AS3FXXD3KB,C340152* was added to bc.json to fix a bug with *AS3FXXD3KB,C3401* for a specific model. So, it seems we want the 2nd example (*ectool bcfg search bc.json AS3FXXD3KB C340152 345*) to pass: the more specific config (*AS3FXXD3KB,C340152*) should be used.\n\nIf *AS3FXXD3KB,C3401* is meant to be used, *AS3FXXD3KB,C340152* should have been removed from bc.json. So, I assume the more specific match should be always the intended one.\n\nWhen multiple matches are found, I think we should print \u0027warning: multiple matches were found\u0027 or ask the user for confirmation.\n\nWhat\u0027s your thought?",
